--- reading it
    1xN (1 reference, N queries) and Nx1 (N references, 1 query) are both N cells, so
    the two columns separate query-side from reference-side cost: whichever is larger is
    the side that dominates at this N. Per-cell cost falling with N is fixed
    per-invocation cost being amortised, not a scaling penalty. Peak RSS is a per-process
    high-water mark.

